course: dictionary
lesson: 1638
title: Childhood in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word childhood is a noun. It means the time when a person is a child, and it can also mean the kind of life someone had as a child. Context helps you choose the right meaning. «Old card and board games from grandparents' childhoods are still fun to play today.» Here childhoods means the times when the grandparents were children.
explain: Clue words near childhood show you its meaning. Words like «happy» and «friend» tell you it is about being a child. Try the swap check: put "the time when I was a child" in place of childhood and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Grown-ups often talk about their own childhood. «Grown-ups give these rules out of love and from their own childhood, and some are half right.» Here childhood means the years when the grown-ups were children, so their rules come partly from their own experiences.
fact: Childhood is a noun, so it names a time or a kind of life.
fact: Childhood means the time of a person's life when they are a child.
fact: A childhood means the kind of life someone had as a child, such as «a happy childhood».
fact: Phrases like «childhood friend», «childhood memories» and «early childhood» use the same word.
fact: Childhood comes before being a teenager and an adult.
exercise: «Old card and board games from grandparents' childhoods are still fun to play today.» What does childhoods mean here? | Grandparents who are very old | *The times when the grandparents were children | Games sold in shops | Toys they gave away
exercise: Sam says, «My childhood friend lives next door.» What does childhood show? | A friend who lives in a castle | A friend who is a teacher | *A friend from when Sam was a child | A friend Sam has never met
exercise: «Many childhood injuries happen when children are bored and try risky things to pass the time.» Find and copy one word that means hurts to the body. | children | *injuries | happen | bored
test: «Brains change as you learn, which is called plasticity, especially fast in childhood.» When do brains change fastest here? | *In childhood | Never | At night | In old age
test: What is a childhood? | *The kind of life someone had as a child | A grown-up's job | A type of school subject | A big house with a garden
exam: Which is the best meaning of childhood? | A grey, wet day | A kind of food | *The time of a person's life when they are a child | A grown-up's job
